plan
.
. The text plan refers to two independent watch handles 'x', 'y', and 'z'
. that can be associated to paths via 'watch_*'.
.
+ watch_z /a/b/
  .
  . Watch directory, to be triggered whenever entries are added or removed.
  .
+ new_file /a/b/c | : file c, version 1
+ expect_trigger_z

+ watch_x /a/b/c
  .
  . As the file already exists, an initial watch notification is expected.
  .
+ expect_trigger_x

+ watch_y /a/b/d
  .
  . The file 'd' does not exist yet.
  . The watch handle is expected to trigger as soon as the file appears.
  .
+ expect_content /a/b/c | : file c, version 1

+ append /a/b/c | : +
+ expect_trigger_x
+ expect_content /a/b/c | : file c, version 1+

+ new_file /a/b/c | : file c, version 2
+ expect_trigger_x
+ expect_content /a/b/c | : file c, version 2

+ rename /a/b/c | to: /a/b/d
+ expect_trigger_x
+ expect_trigger_y
+ expect_trigger_z
+ expect_missing /a/b/c
+ expect_content /a/b/d | : file c, version 2

+ unlink /a/b/d
+ expect_trigger_y
+ expect_trigger_z
+ expect_missing /a/b/d
-
